UID:127b1af420eb4c54@nutcracker2026
DTSTAMP:20260914T010516Z
SEQUENCE:2026091401
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20261209T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20261209T205000
SUMMARY:Nutcracker: Cast A Dress Rehearsal – ACT II Cast A (Mandatory 
 – Production Week)
LOCATION:Robinson Center
DESCRIPTION:Wed. Dec. 9 · Call 7:30 PM · 8:10 PM–8:50 PM · Robinson 
 Center\nMANDATORY — production week. CALL TIME 7:30 PM: dancers must b
 e checked in and backstage by then\, so arrive by 7:15 PM. BA: Call Time
  is the time dancers should be check-in and backstage - Arrive 15 minute
 s before Call Time.\nACT II Dress Run\; In Performance Costumes\, Hair a
 nd Makeup.\nAll Casts are called unless a cast is named. SUBJECT TO CHAN
 GE — the BA master schedule\, the weekly BA emails and the BA portal a
 re the official source. Master: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1
 xWFCPfY5m0aK9d5dnxvALNre-6-N7Cl0kkw24rvm6cE/\n\nCOSTUME / HAIR / MAKEUP 
 for Bon Bons: Mother Ginger's Bon Bons — Costume (you provide): Pink S
 eamless Tights\, Flesh-tone camisole leotard\; Shoes: Pink Ballet Shoes 
 *Dancers of Color may wear flesh-tone ballet shoes\; Makeup: Light Stage
  Makeup\; Hair: High Bun\, No Part\; Accessories (BA provides): Pink Hat
 \; Prop (BA provides): Lollipop\nLight Stage Makeup Instruction Sheet:\n
 •  Powder matching skintone\n•  Light brown eye shadow applied
  to the crease with an eye shadow brush\n•  Dark Brown/Black eyelin
 er and black mascara. No fake lashes.\n•  Blush on the cheeks (be s
 ure to apply plenty so dancer doesn’t look washed out in the stage lig
 hts)\n•  Red or Dark Red lipstick\nDancers of Color may wear flesh 
 tone tights and flesh tone ballet shoes.\nCostume Care Guidelines:\n• 
  Handle costume pieces with care while changing to prevent damage to 
 delicate fabrics\n•  Promptly notify Ballet Arkansas in the event o
 f costume damage at the point of discovery\, no matter how significant\n
 •  Never throw costumes or accessories on the floor\, or hang costu
 mes by their elastic straps\n•  Refrain from sitting on the floor w
 hile in costume\n•  Do not attempt to alter\, mend\, clean\, or lau
 nder any costume or accessory\n•  Never apply stage make-up while i
 n costume and shall take great care to refrain from smudging make-up on 
 costume during its removal\n•  Refrain from the use of spray perfum
 e or cologne while in costume\n•  Never wear any garment not assign
 ed to cast member\n•  Do not handle or consume food or beverage whi
 le in costume\, with the exception of water\n•  Do not remove costu
 mes from their assigned dressing rooms or from the theater\n•  Remo
 ve all bobby pins used to secure head pieces and wigs following their us
 e\n•  Return all headpieces to their assigned bags\n•  Comply 
 fully with any and all updates to Ballet Arkansas’ wardrobe policies\n
 •  Do not pack markers\, paints\, colored drinks or anything that m
 ay damage or stain costumes.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT1H
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Nutcracker in 1 hour
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
